    "physical_description": "Skirt cloth, the body (badan) hand-painted and dyed in the batik process in brown and blue on a buff-coloured ground with a repeating pattern of diagonal saw-edge stripes, of which every alternate pair of teeth are curved into a circle from which projects a triangle whose apex is elongated in a curved line terminating in a loop. The front piece (kapala) is 'capped' or wax-printed with copper blocks in a design of a flowering tree with birds and butterflies, and dyed red.",
